{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"git show 961f9e47:docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml | Select-String -Pattern '\"'^'\"\\\\[requirement.SR-161\\\\]' -Context 0,19; git show 961f9e47:docs/test/inspection-procedures.md | Select-String -Pattern '\"'^##.*[Dd]ecomposition|''^###.*[Dd]ecomposition|Missing perspective outcome'\"' -Context 0,28; git show 9f2080d3a8e0feaadf0c60b3e8a8ed3d55357c49:docs/rubrics/plan-decomposition.md | Measure-Object -Line; git rev-parse HEAD\"","aggregated_output":"\r\n> [requirement.SR-161]\r\n  title = \"Decompositions carry a perspective record\"\r\n  sn_refs = [\"SN-036\"]\r\n  boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\n  hat_refs = [\"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\r\n  requirement = \"\"\"When a decomposition round is reviewed, the delivered planning content shall provide every \r\napplicable declared perspective's question in the decomposition brief and require the sitting's review record to name \r\nthe outcome for each perspective.\"\"\"\r\n  rationale = \"\"\"A decomposition produced from one perspective can look complete while omitting security, operations \r\nor first-use failures. The hats roster and plan briefs already supply the applicable questions, and the sitting's \r\nreview record preserves their outcomes; a separate machine-readable coverage record and checker would duplicate that \r\nreview without improving its adequacy judgment. Hat-Refs remain the row-level provenance for perspectives that raised \r\na requirement. This applies the owner ruling of 2026-09-06 (docs/log.d/2026-09-06-sn036-owner-ruling.md).\"\"\"\r\n  acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"For one completed decomposition round, the applicable perspectives resolve from the \r\ndeclared hats roster, the decomposition brief presents each applicable perspective's question, and the sitting's \r\nreview record names an outcome for every one; the independent adequacy review reads that record.\"\"\"\r\n  priority = \"S\"\r\n  verification = \"Inspection\"\r\n  status = \"Approved\"\r\n  phase = 5\r\n  \r\n  [requirement.SR-162]\r\n  title = \"Requirement boundary references resolve against the declared frame\"\r\n  sn_refs = [\"SN-037\"]\r\n  boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\r\n  hat_refs = [\"TEST-ENGINEER\"]\r\n  requirement = \"\"\"The delivered harness shall resolve every system-requirement boundary reference, and every declared \r\ninterface's endpoint pair and signal type, against the declared external frame — an unresolvable crossing failing the \r\nstrict trace naming the row — reporting requirements naming no crossing, crossings named by no requirement, declared \r\ncrossings with no realizing interface row, an interface declaring no endpoint pair or no signal type from the closed \r\ndiscrete/variable vocabulary, and a seam joined to a counterpart whose signal type is incompatible with its own, each \r\nas an advisory, and staying vacuous for a project declaring no frame.\"\"\"\r\n  rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-037 — every promised behavior's entry and exit locatable at a declared boundary, \r\nunresolved references mechanical findings, in the need's own words. SN-037 had no citing SR even though the machinery \r\nis already delivered (the frame registry, the boundary-reference field, the resolution and coverage rules); this row \r\nis the obligation that machinery enforces. Severity split deliberately: resolution hard, coverage advisory — the ruled \r\nwarn-first sequencing while the corpus converges. The row also carries SN-037's SIGNAL-TYPING half — \"every referenced \r\ninterface identifies its boundary endpoints and whether its signal is discrete or variable ... incompatible signal \r\ntypes are mechanical findings\". That half had ZERO textual occurrence in the SR layer while `orphans=0` held, even \r\nthough `interfaces.toml` already carries a `signal` cell on every row (many of them typed `variable` by a recorded \r\ndefault with a re-type note, which is exactly the state a check is owed for). NAMED RESIDUAL, stated rather than \r\nquietly dropped: the need's last clause — that a reviewed change altering one side of the requirement/interface \r\nrelationship carries or justifies the corresponding change on the other — is a REVIEW obligation this row does not \r\nclaim to mechanize.\"\"\"\r\n> ## Decomposition proportionality inspection\r\n  \r\n  Read one actual completed decomposition review record, the declared hats roster,\r\n  and the decomposition brief used by that review. Resolve the applicable hats,\r\n  confirm that the brief presents every applicable hat's question and that the\r\n  review record names each hat's outcome. Confirm the required spine remains the\r\n  scope boundary, then inspect the complete reviewed chain and a small chain\r\n  containing a child that only paraphrases or duplicates a parent's decision or\r\n  verification. A missing applicable-hat outcome or a child within a required tier\r\n  with no independent decision or verification purpose is an Inspection finding.\r\n  Record why further splitting stops at the independent-value boundary. This\r\n  procedure uses the existing brief and review record and does not impose a\r\n  row-count threshold, extra depth, new record carrier, or machine coverage check.\r\n  \r\n> ### Decomposition proportionality inspection result\r\n  \r\n  **PASS — 2026-09-06, [fresh Opus 5/high Inspection](../reviews/2026-09-06-sn036-inspection-structured-opus.md).** \r\nThe independent inspector re-derived the\r\n  applicable set from the roster and exact parent/work context, confirmed every\r\n  applicable question in the [actual brief](../reviews/2026-09-06-sn036-decomposition-brief.md),\r\n  and read a reasoned outcome for each in the [completed \r\nreview](../reviews/2026-09-06-sn036-closure-structured-opus.md).\r\n  It checked the chain's distinct child purposes, the permitted direct Inspection\r\n  tiers and the stated stopping reason. It rejected the missing TEST-ENGINEER\r\n  outcome and the paraphrasing-child cases. This is document Inspection evidence;\r\n  it does not approve artifact text or claim software-test execution.\r\n  \r\n  The inspector separately requested corrections to the review's transcribed\r\n  rubric digest, the preflight and the adjudication ledger. The\r\n  [disposition record](../reviews/2026-09-06-sn036-review-dispositions.md) records\r\n  those corrections; the original verdict bodies and historical result remain.\r\n  The extra negative brief-question example is a queued future improvement, not\r\n  an execution claimed here.\r\n  \r\n  **Historical INCOMPLETE — 2026-09-06, [earlier Opus 5/high \r\nInspection](../reviews/2026-09-06-oi85-inspection-structured-opus.md).** That inspector accepted the\r\n  independent purposes of SR-184/SR-185/SR-186 and their direct Inspection cases,\r\n  read the stopping reason, and rejected the paraphrasing child. The procedure\r\n  then required a machine-produced SR-161 perspective record that did not exist,\r\n  as LLR-183 then stated. The later [owner \r\nruling](../log.md#2026-09-06--sn-036--sr-161-owner-ruling-review-pass-not-a-guard)\r\n  replaced that obligation with the existing hat-by-hat review path; this sitting\r\n  amended LLR-183 accordingly. The earlier result remains incomplete for the\r\n  procedure it actually executed. A new Inspection of the revised procedure is\r\n  recorded separately; the ruling itself supplies no test result.\r\n  \r\n  ## Bounded abnormal inspection inputs\r\n> - **Missing perspective outcome:** the actual completed review record with its\r\n    TEST-ENGINEER outcome omitted, while the applicable-hat brief and all other\r\n    outcomes remain. The Inspection must identify that omitted applicable hat.\r\n  - **Paraphrasing child:** the actual SR-186→TC-211 chain gains an unminted\r\n    candidate child saying “the process shall keep decomposition proportionate,”\r\n    verified by the same Inspection judgment without another decision or case.\r\n    Its only stated purpose is to make the chain look more detailed. This adds\r\n    no independent decision or verification purpose within a required tier.\r\n  \r\n  The historical incomplete result records what that earlier inspection examined.\r\n  The later TC-211 execution above inspected the actual completed review record\r\n  and recorded its own reviewer, date, subject and findings; the owner ruling\r\n  itself supplied no Inspection result.\r\n\r\nLines      : 78\r\nWords      : \r\nCharacters : \r\nProperty   : \r\n\r\n9f2080d3a8e0feaadf0c60b3e8a8ed3d55357c49\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
